%N A401476 Primes p such that 2^p - 2 is a primitive practical number.
%C A401476 Conjecture: The sequence has infinitely many terms. In other words, there are infinitely many primitive practical numbers of the form 2^p - 2 with p prime.
%C A401476 By Fermat's little theorem, p divides 2^p - 2 for any prime p.
%C A401476 The first nonsquarefree primitive practical number of the form 2^p - 2, with p prime, occurs at p = 103.
%H A401476 Frank M Jackson, <a href="/A401476/a401476.txt">Mathematica program</a>
%e A401476 a(3) = 5, because 2^5 - 2 = 30 and 30 is a primitive practical number.
